CORRECTED 2026-10-07: the reader's database engine is now turso_core
0.8.2 (https://github.com/tursodatabase/turso, MIT, Copyright (c) the
Turso authors), a pure-Rust reimplementation of SQLite, on every target.
Its dependency tree (checked with `cargo tree`, 2026-10-07) is under MIT,
Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, BSL-1.0 and Unicode-3.0 licences
(each, or one option of each dual licence, compatible with AGPL-3.0).
rusqlite (MIT) with SQLite (public domain, through libsqlite3-sys, MIT) is
a native-only dev-dependency: the tests build Zotero databases with real
SQLite and compare the reader against it. No SQLite C code is shipped.
The rollback-journal "hot journal" test in src/zotero/local_library/db.rs
follows SQLite's pager.c hasHotJournal (SQLite 3.53.2, public domain).

