Code-to-code verification ran upstream (maintainer authorisation,
2026-10-07): a Zotero translation-server on 127.0.0.1:1969, and (#749) the
same translation-server code loaded into the reference script's own Node
process, to force an import translator or export to a format the server has
no name for. What it returned
is committed under tests/data/zotero/reference/ (scripts/zotero-reference.sh;
manifest.json records the commits). Those files contain upstream's output and,
as test inputs, upstream data:

  * every `testCases` entry of BibTeX.js, RIS.js and CSL JSON.js
    (translators commit above; AGPL-3.0-or-later);
  * every import `testCases` entry of the #749 translators above
    (ReferBibIX.js, RefWorks Tagged.js, Bookmarks.js, MEDLINEnbib.js, OVID
    Tagged.js, Web of Science Tagged.js, Datacite JSON.js, OpenAlex JSON.js;
    same commit and licences). They carry bibliographic metadata as the
    translator authors recorded it (PubMed, OVID, Web of Science, DataCite
    and OpenAlex records of published works);
  * zotero/test/tests/data/itemJSON.js (Zotero commit 9cbba8c4d281, via
    kovan-common's tests/data/zotero/itemJSON.json; AGPL-3.0-or-later);
  * tests/data/zotero/fixtures/import/book_and_child_note.ris, copied from
    zotero/test/tests/data/book_and_child_note.ris (Zotero commit
    9cbba8c4d281; AGPL-3.0-or-later).

The other fixtures in tests/data/zotero/fixtures/ were written for kovan
(2026-10-07) and contain no third-party data.
